property rights therein. No ownership or co-ownership of the Toolkit
is transferred to You by this license or by access to the Toolkit's
repository. All rights not expressly granted in Section 4 are
reserved by the Licensor.

This license grants no rights in the Licensor's names, marks, logos,
or branding, including "FDK", "Faded Dream ToolKit", and "Faded
Dream".

3. SCOPE — WHAT THIS LICENSE GOVERNS

This license governs the Toolkit and the materials expressly covered
by it. It does NOT automatically govern Applications. Applications
built with the Toolkit are governed by their authors' own licenses
and terms, by applicable law, by any separate agreements that apply
to them, and by the licenses of any third-party components their
authors include. Nothing in this license is intended to reach into,
restrict, or claim rights over independent Application code or
assets, as further described in Section 5.

4. LICENSE GRANT

Subject to the terms of this license, the Licensor grants You a
limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable license to:

  a. Download, install, and use the Toolkit, and to make the copies
     of it (including backup copies) that are reasonably necessary to
     do so, for the purpose of developing, building, testing, and
     running Applications;

  b. Build Applications that link against, bind, or otherwise
     incorporate the Toolkit;

  c. Distribute and commercially sell or otherwise exploit Your
     Applications, subject to Section 5; and

  d. Distribute Runtime Copies as part of Your Applications,
     provided that each such Runtime Copy is unmodified, retains all
     copyright, trademark, and other proprietary notices, is
     distributed solely as incorporated into and required to execute
     an Application, is not distributed separately from an
     Application or as a standalone library, toolkit, SDK, component,
     or asset package, and is not itself the subject of a charge
     attributable to the Toolkit.

  [REVIEW: Section 4(d) implements a "runtime accompaniment" model —
  Applications may carry the unmodified FDK runtime they need. If the
  Licensor instead intends that end users obtain the Toolkit runtime
  separately, this subsection should be removed or narrowed, and
  Section 5 adjusted accordingly.]

5. APPLICATIONS AND DEVELOPER RIGHTS

  a. Applications are independent works. To the maximum extent
     permitted by applicable law, this license claims no rights over
     Applications, and the Licensor neither owns nor co-owns an
     Application by virtue of its author having used the Toolkit to
     build it.

  b. You retain all rights in and to Your Applications, including
     their source code, assets, branding, and licensing. You may
     distribute, license, sell, or otherwise exploit Your
     Applications under terms You choose, subject to applicable law,
     to any separate agreements that bind You, and to the licenses of
     third-party components You include in them.

  c. Applications do not become the property of the Licensor or of
     the Faded Dream Project merely because they use FDK. The
     restrictions of Section 6 attach to the Toolkit, never to
     independent Application code or assets.

  d. Nothing in this license limits Your right to state factually
     that Your Application is built with FDK. However, You may not
     name, brand, or market Your Application in a way that states or
     implies that it IS the Toolkit, that it is part of the Faded
     Dream Project, or that the Licensor endorses it, without prior
     Written Authorization.

  e. The boundary: if You extract, adapt, or republish Toolkit code,
     Toolkit components, or Toolkit assets outside of an Application
     — for example, as another toolkit, framework, library, template,
     or asset collection — that act is governed by Section 6, not by
     this Section.

6. RESTRICTIONS ON THE TOOLKIT

Except as expressly permitted by Section 4, or by separate Written
Authorization, You may NOT:

  a. Copy or redistribute the Toolkit, in source or object form,
     including publishing, uploading, mirroring, or packaging it for
     third parties — in whole or in part, original or modified;

  b. Modify, adapt, translate, or create derivative works of the
     Toolkit, or distribute a Toolkit modified by You or for You;

  c. Sublicense, sell, rent, lease, lend, or otherwise transfer
     rights in the Toolkit to any third party;

  d. Commercially exploit the Toolkit itself — including charging for
     access to it, offering it as a product or hosted service, or
     building a competing toolkit, framework, or SDK upon it. This
     subsection restricts the Toolkit; it does NOT restrict the
     commercial distribution or sale of Applications, which Section
     4(c) expressly permits;

  e. Remove, obscure, or alter any copyright, trademark, or other
     proprietary notice contained in the Toolkit or in a Runtime Copy;

  f. Reverse engineer, decompile, or disassemble the Toolkit, except
     to the extent such acts are expressly permitted by mandatory
     applicable law notwithstanding this restriction [REVIEW: the
     scope of this carve-out is jurisdiction-dependent];

  g. Use the Toolkit's shipped assets (including its theme faces)
     outside of an Application, or redistribute them as standalone
     theme or asset packages.

Access to the Toolkit's repository — including cloning it, reading
its source, or building it locally — grants only the rights in this
license. Such access does not grant any right to redistribute, reuse,
repackage, or sublicense the Toolkit beyond Sections 4 and 5, and does
not constitute ownership of any kind.

